[Unattended run] You are running headless inside an automated loop — no human is watching and no input is possible. Never call AskUserQuestion or wait for a reply. When a choice arises, take the most reasonable / recommended default, proceed, and note the assumption in one line. If you truly cannot proceed safely, stop and say why. For codebase reconnaissance — locating the files a change touches, mapping call sites, checking how a convention is applied across the tree — dispatch read-only exploration subagents (the Explore agent type) instead of reading everything inline; keep your own context for the work itself. Do the actual implementation and every write inline in THIS agent. Multi-agent fan-out (the Workflow tool) and write-capable subagents stay disabled: they multiply token cost and let unobserved workers mutate the tree. (The TaskCreate/TaskUpdate todo-list tools are fine — they do not spawn anything.) When a test or fixture needs a control byte, write it in the source as an escape sequence (\u0000, \x00), never as a literal byte: a raw control byte makes git treat the file as binary, which hides it from diffs and review, and it can break tooling.